// Athens County, Ohio — curated directory of meaningful links.
// Single source of truth for the app. Keep entries verified and current.
// Fields: name, category, subcategory, url, description
// Last reviewed: 2026-11-09
//
// Every URL below was fetched and its content checked against the organization
// it claims to be. Sites that block automated fetching (the Board of Elections,
// the Auditor's search, the health department, the chamber, ACEnet, Rural
// Action, Stuart's Opera House, the music festival, United Seniors, Baileys and
// Canaan Township) were checked in a browser.
//
// THE HAZARD HERE IS ATHENS, GEORGIA
//
// Athens-Clarke County, GA dominates every search. Athens Christian School and
// the Athens Montessori hits are Georgia; athenschamber.ORG is Athens,
// TENNESSEE (ours is athenschamber.com). hnlcpa.com/port is Licking County.
//
// THINGS THAT ARE OUT OF DATE EVERYWHERE ELSE
//
//   * The Athens NEWS stopped printing in January 2026 and its site now
//     redirects to the Messenger's archive. Not listed.
//   * The county fair is athenscofair.org; athenscountyfair.org does not resolve.
//     unitedappealathens.org and bbbsathens.com do not resolve either, and
//     211athenscounty.org loads blank.
//   * stroudsrunstatepark.com is a third-party StateParks.com site; the ODNR
//     page is used. HAPCAP is hapcap.org, not Facebook.
//   * The Farm Bureau is now Athens-Meigs (office in Pomeroy).
//   * WATH/WXTQ were sold in 2023 to Total Media; WAIS 770 now simulcasts
//     The Wolf (Lancaster). WEAK 106.7 went dark in 2023.
//   * Tri-County Career Center moved to tricounty.cc; ISBH to isbh.org (its old
//     domain is for sale); the state hospital page moved to dbh.ohio.gov.
//   * The county portal's solid-waste link goes to the nonprofit Athens-Hocking
//     Recycling Centers; the district itself is ahswd.org. Its Engineer link
//     (.com) is stale; the live site is athenscountyengineer.org.
//
// GEOGRAPHY
//
//   * Two cities (Athens, Nelsonville), eight villages, fourteen townships.
//     Buchtel, Coolville, Glouster and Trimble have no village sites; only
//     Athens, Ames, Canaan and Rome townships have sites.
//   * Many county offices are not in Athens: EMA, 911, SWCD and Veterans in The
//     Plains; JFS and CSEA in Millfield; the dog shelter in Chauncey. Athens
//     City Schools' office is in Chauncey; the library system is headquartered
//     in Nelsonville.
//   * There is no county building department and no county zoning.
//   * Burr Oak State Park is mostly in Morgan County; Lake Hope is in Vinton
//     County (excluded). Buckeye Hills Regional Council is in Marietta.
//   * WOUB (Ohio University) is the local public TV and radio station.
//
// LEFT OUT rather than listed unverified: the Clerk's CourtView, the Land Bank
// (no site), United Appeal/211 and Big Brothers Big Sisters (dead or blank
// sites), Rotary, the Uptown Business Association and ORCA (no sites), OhioHealth
// hospice in Athens (no first-party Athens page), Heritage Christian School
// (church site only) and the villages and townships named above.

